From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:57:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: name the check behind every SUBMIT rejection

A bare EINVAL from DRM_IOCTL_ASAHI_SUBMIT reached userspace as device
loss with nothing in the kernel log (gfxrecon --dump-resources replay,
replaydump-kit2-20261024), leaving 29 candidate checks. Route every
EINVAL/ENOTSUPP of submit(), its timestamp resolver, render_parameters(),
compute_parameters() and the mapping check through reject()/unsupported(),
which log "G16: SUBMIT rejected with <errno>: <check and values> (<comm>
pid <tgid>)" for the first 32 rejections of the boot, then one line saying
further ones are only counted. Every rejection is counted in debugfs
dep_stats (submit_rejected). Return values are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
